Error [jet.ModuleValueNotBuilt]: `EARLY` can't be computed while building: it calls `left`, which reads `context`, the task context of the code that runs it
  --> tests/ui/module_value_reads_the_task_context.jet:4:8
    |
  4 | EARLY: left(5)
    |        ^^^^^^^
 Why: A module-level `name: value` is computed while building and stored in the program, the same value on every tier; no code runs before `run: fn`, so a value that stops, reaches the outside world, or can't run while building is a build error
 Fix: Compute it in `run` and pass it on; or make it a function, marked `#Memo` when it is pure so the first result is kept; or, for outside data, read a pinned build input such as `#run { embed_file("config.txt") }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0643
